<title>ARGENTINA: Brazil's Malan rules out big devaluation - interview.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Malan rules out big devaluation - interview.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Finance Minister, Pedro Malan, dismissed the possibility of a large devaluation of the real, according to an interview published Monday in the Argentine daily newspaper La Nacion.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be no return to protectionism nor a 'maxidevaluation' of the real - I want to insist on this to my Argentine friends and readers,&quot; Malan was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>Many Argentine analysts consider a major devaluation in neighboring Brazil as the biggest threat to the stability of Argentina's economy.</p>
</text>
